<%# The filter bar rebuilt along the Belegungstabelle (doc/filterleiste_s1_s4_plan.md).
    Row 1: the saved views as tabs (F10), the base view first, then "+ Filter" (F2)
    and the search (F35). Row 2: one pill per condition (F13), rendered by the
    Stimulus controller, gone while there is none. Row 3: the save row (F23).
    No offset against the page header and no horizontal padding: the tab row sits
    flush with the page title and the list surface below (header unification 2026-07). %>
<%# The list's workbench: a raised surface (the same step the times list's
    filter stripe makes), one hairline below, no radius and no border - that is
    the language of dropdowns.
    ⚠️ No side margins and no side padding of its own. It sets its width from
    the column it is rendered into, and a head reaches exactly as far as the
    thing it belongs to. Full bleed here (which it had briefly) made it span
    both columns, so the column tool stood over the detail lane although it is
    the list that has columns. Tint stays reserved for "selected". %>
<div class="filter-bar relative z-sticky bg-surface-raised border-b border-cream-300 pt-2 flex flex-col mb-3.5"
     data-controller="filter-bar"
     data-filter-bar-return-keys-value="<%= return_keys.to_json %>"
     data-filter-bar-url-value="<%= base_url %>"
     data-filter-bar-view-key-value="<%= view_key %>"
     data-filter-bar-type-targets-value="<%= type_targets.to_json %>"
     data-filter-bar-frame-value="<%= frame_id %>"
     data-filter-bar-categories-value="<%= categories_json_for_bar %>"
     data-filter-bar-active-filters-value="<%= ad_hoc_filters.to_json %>"
     data-filter-bar-active-operators-value="<%= ad_hoc_operators.to_json %>"
     data-filter-bar-dropped-value="<%= dropped_categories.to_json %>"
     data-filter-bar-labels-value="<%= filter_bar_labels_json %>"
     data-filter-bar-operator-labels-value="<%= operator_labels_json %>"
     data-filter-bar-save-url-value="<%= save_smart_folder_path %>"
     data-filter-bar-project-id-value="<%= project&.id %>"
     data-filter-bar-save-labels-value="<%= save_labels_json %>"
     data-filter-bar-search-mode-value="<%= search_mode %>"
     data-filter-bar-smart-folder-id-value="<%= active_smart_folder&.id %>"
     data-filter-bar-smart-folders-value="<%= smart_folders_json %>"
     data-filter-bar-dissolver-value="<%= dissolver_data_json %>"
     data-filter-bar-value-labels-value="<%= value_labels_json %>">

  <%# === ROW 1: view tabs + "+ Filter" + search === %>
  <%# The strip carries -mb-px so the active tab's 2 px ink line lies ON the row's
      1 px divider instead of above it; a negative margin on the tabs themselves
      would be clipped by the strip's overflow. data-fb-tabrow lets the row wrap
      narrow, when the open search takes a line of its own (components/filter_bar.css). %>
  <div class="flex items-end gap-2 min-h-[40px] border-b border-divider" data-fb-tabrow>
    <%# The views (F10). Each tab is a link to the view's address, so it works
        without JavaScript; the action only carries the typed search along.
        Only the first few stand here, the rest folds into the menu beside them
        (20a, D1). The strip keeps its scroll as the narrow fallback: five short
        tabs fit a desk and not a phone, and rule 7 says leave out or move, not
        shrink. %>
    <div role="tablist"
         aria-label="<%= t('components.filter_bar.view_tabs_label') %>"
         <%# No flex-1: the strip takes the width of its tabs and no more, so the
             tools sit right behind them. With flex-1 it swallowed the whole row
             and pushed them flush right, where they wander with the content
             width and end up standing over the detail lane. It may still SHRINK
             (min-w-0 plus the default flex-shrink), which is what keeps the
             overflow scroll working on a narrow head. %>
         class="flex items-end gap-0.5 min-w-0 overflow-x-auto scrollbar-hide -mb-px"
         data-filter-bar-target="tabStrip">
      <% visible_views.each do |view| %>
        <%# The active tab is a slot: the link, then the chevron (F22) that opens
            the menu of the view. Two targets (designer, 09.09.2026): the word
            chooses the view, the chevron opens its menu. The ink line lies under
            the WORD alone, as its mark; the chevron stands beside it without
            one, vertically centred. Only the active tab has the chevron, the
            base view too. %>
        <span class="inline-flex items-center flex-shrink-0">
          <a href="<%= view[:url] %>"
             role="tab"
             aria-selected="<%= view[:active] %>"
             data-filter-bar-target="tab"
             data-action="click->filter-bar#selectView"
             class="<%= tab_classes(view[:active]) %>">
            <% if view[:badge_icon] %>
              <i class="bi <%= view[:badge_icon] %> text-[10px] opacity-60" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <% end %>
            <span data-view-name><%= view[:name] %></span>
            <% if view[:active] && (view[:id] || view[:key]) %>
              <%# F23: the amber dot for "not saved yet". Only a saved view (a folder
                  or a built-in type view) can hold a change; the base view has
                  nothing to differ from. Shown by the controller. %>
              <span data-filter-bar-target="unsavedDot"
                    class="hidden h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-amber-500"
                    title="<%= t('components.filter_bar.unsaved') %>"></span>
            <% end %>
          </a>
          <% if view[:active] %>
            <%# A tile of 28 x 28 (grid, centred), not padding around a glyph:
                with padding alone the hit area fell under 24px. The one chevron
                of the row: "n weitere" is a listing of its own and the search
                a magnifier, neither wears one any more, so this one is not
                confused with them. %>
            <button type="button"
                    data-action="click->filter-bar#toggleViewMenu"
                    data-filter-bar-target="viewMenuButton"
                    aria-haspopup="dialog"
                    aria-expanded="false"
                    aria-label="<%= t('components.filter_bar.view_menu') %>"
                    title="<%= t('components.filter_bar.view_menu') %>"
                    class="<%= CHEVRON_TILE_CLASSES %>">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="11" height="11" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7"
                   stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="transition-transform"
                   data-filter-bar-target="viewMenuChevron" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M3.5 6l4.5 4.5L12.5 6" />
              </svg>
            </button>
          <% end %>
        </span>
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <%# The views that did not fit (20a, D1). The trigger stands OUTSIDE the
        scrolling strip, so it cannot scroll away with what it is hiding, and
        its layer needs no head: "2 weitere" already says what is in it. %>
    <% if overflow_views.any? %>
      <div class="relative flex-shrink-0">
        <button type="button"
                data-action="click->filter-bar#toggleOverflowMenu"
                data-filter-bar-target="overflowButton"
                data-fb-overflow
                aria-haspopup="menu"
                aria-expanded="false"
                class="h-8 px-2 text-[13px] font-normal rounded-md text-muted hover:text-heading hover:bg-cream-100
                       transition-colors inline-flex items-center gap-1.5
                       focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ink">
          <%# The word alone (designer, 09.09.2026): "n weitere" is a listing,
              not a second kind of opener, and the row's one chevron belongs to
              the active tab. %>
          <%= t('components.filter_bar.more_views', count: overflow_views.size) %>
        </button>

        <div data-filter-bar-target="overflowMenu"
             role="menu"
             aria-label="<%= t('components.filter_bar.more_views', count: overflow_views.size) %>"
             class="hidden absolute left-0 top-full mt-1 w-56 bg-surface-raised border border-cream-300 rounded-lg shadow-md z-dropdown p-1">
          <% overflow_views.each do |view| %>
            <a href="<%= view[:url] %>"
               role="menuitem"
               data-action="click->filter-bar#selectView"
               class="<%= MENU_ROW_CLASSES %>"><%= view[:name] %></a>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>
    <% end %>

    <%# The tools of this list, as ONE group at the RIGHT END of the row
        (designer, 07.09.2026): narrow it down, search it, choose its columns.
        ms-auto rather than a spacer element - the group has an edge to sit on,
        it does not need something pushing it.
        self-center: the row is items-end so the tabs keep their bottom edge and
        the active tab's underline lands on the row's hairline. The tools have no
        business on that line, so they sit centred ABOVE it.
        ⚠️ It does not wander with the content width, although it is flush right:
        the row ends at the LIST column's edge (the head lives inside that
        column), so its right edge is the list's. %>
    <%# Three tools of equal rank in ONE group (designer, 09.09.2026): filter,
        magnifier, columns, 4px apart, all 28px high; the filter word too,
        which used to stand lower than the icon tiles. %>
    <div class="ms-auto self-center flex items-center gap-1" data-fb-tools>
    <%# "+ Filter" is a secondary action (F2), rounded-md and not a pill: a pill
          is a condition, and this trigger makes one. No count badge; the
          conditions themselves stand in the row below.

          It stands FLAT, without the edge F2 gives a secondary action elsewhere:
          in a toolbar exactly one element wears the fassung of an input field,
          and that is the field (F40, revised 07.09.2026). Three framed boxes of
          which one can be typed into hide the only difference that matters. What
          stays bound is the height, the radius and the font size. %>
      <div class="relative flex-shrink-0">
        <%# Tight (components/filter_bar.css, 760px) the word and its plus are
            left out and the funnel stands in their place, 32 px like the
            magnifier and the column tool beside it. The funnel, because it is
            the sign the app already uses for filtering; not the sliders, which
            are the column tool next door (F39: one symbol, one meaning). A
            sign carries its word in the title, with the count: "Filter · 2
            Bedingungen". The server writes it for the first paint, the
            controller keeps it current on every state render (_renderAddSign),
            because the bar lives outside the frame that reloads. D2 of
            doc/kanban_ticket_als_bahn_plan.md, S5. %>
        <button type="button"
                data-action="click->filter-bar#toggleFilterMenu"
                data-filter-bar-target="filterButton"
                data-fb-add
                aria-haspopup="true"
                aria-expanded="false"
                aria-label="<%= filter_sign_title %>"
                title="<%= filter_sign_title %>"
                class="h-7 px-2 text-[13px] font-normal rounded-md text-body
                       hover:bg-cream-100 hover:text-heading transition-colors inline-flex items-center gap-1.5
                       focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ink">
          <i class="bi bi-plus-lg text-xs" aria-hidden="true" data-fb-add-plus></i>
          <span data-fb-add-label><%= scoped_t('filter_bar.add_filter') %></span>
          <i class="bi bi-funnel text-sm" aria-hidden="true" data-fb-add-sign></i>
        </button>

      </div>

    <%# The search (F35): a magnifier of 28 x 28 that grows into a field on a
          click, at every width (designer, 09.09.2026; the rule
          components/filter_bar.css applied to tight containers only): the size
          follows the frequency, not the room. Searching is a rare act and must
          not be the largest element of the tool group. The field opens at the
          right end of THIS row; a term already typed keeps it open. Inside the
          open field the magnifier is the search-depth trigger where more than
          one depth exists, without a chevron. %>
      <div class="relative flex-shrink-0"
           data-filter-bar-target="search"
           data-fb-search<%= ' data-fb-search-open' if search_value.present? %>>
        <button type="button"
                data-action="click->filter-bar#openSearch"
                data-fb-search-open-button
                aria-label="<%= scoped_t('filter_bar.search_placeholder') %>"
                title="<%= scoped_t('filter_bar.search_placeholder') %>"
                class="grid place-items-center h-7 w-7 rounded-md text-muted hover:bg-cream-100 hover:text-heading transition-colors
                       focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ink">
          <i class="bi bi-search text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        </button>
        <% if show_search_depth_selector? %>
          <button type="button"
                  data-action="click->filter-bar#toggleSearchDepthMenu"
                  data-filter-bar-target="searchDepthButton"
                  data-fb-depth
                  aria-haspopup="true"
                  aria-expanded="false"
                  aria-label="<%= scoped_t('filter_bar.search_depth_label') %>"
                  class="absolute inset-y-0 left-0 flex items-center pl-2.5 pr-1 text-faint hover:text-heading transition-colors z-10"
                  title="<%= scoped_t('filter_bar.search_depth_label') %>">
            <i class="bi <%= search_mode_icon %> text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          </button>
        <% else %>
          <span class="absolute inset-y-0 left-0 flex items-center pl-2.5 pr-1 text-faint pointer-events-none z-10" data-fb-depth>
            <i class="bi <%= search_mode_icon %> text-xs"></i>
          </span>
        <% end %>

        <input type="search" name="search"
               data-filter-bar-target="searchInput"
               <%= 'data-keyboard-navigation-target=searchInput' if keyboard_navigation %>
               data-action="input->filter-bar#onSearchInput search->filter-bar#onSearchClear keydown.esc->filter-bar#closeSearch focusout->filter-bar#searchBlur"
               value="<%= search_value %>"
               placeholder="<%= scoped_t('filter_bar.search_placeholder') %>"
               aria-label="<%= scoped_t('filter_bar.search_placeholder') %>"
               autocomplete="off"
               class="w-full h-7 <%= show_search_depth_selector? ? 'pl-9' : 'pl-7' %> pr-2 text-[13px] rounded-md border border-cream-300 bg-surface-raised text-body
                      placeholder:text-faint focus:outline-none focus:border-ink focus:ring-2 focus:ring-ink/10 transition-colors">

        <% if show_search_depth_selector? %>
          <%# Search depth, a floating layer (F29) with F33 rows %>
          <div data-filter-bar-target="searchDepthMenu"
               role="menu"
               aria-label="<%= scoped_t('filter_bar.search_depth_label') %>"
               class="hidden absolute right-0 top-full mt-1 w-56 bg-surface-raised border border-cream-300 rounded-lg shadow-md z-dropdown p-1">
            <div class="px-2 py-1.5 text-[10px] font-semibold text-muted uppercase tracking-wider">
              <%= scoped_t('filter_bar.search_depth_label') %>
            </div>
            <% search_depth_options.each do |mode, icon, label, description| %>
              <button type="button"
                      role="menuitem"
                      data-action="click->filter-bar#setSearchMode"
                      data-mode="<%= mode %>"
                      class="w-full text-left px-2 py-1.5 text-xs text-body hover:bg-cream-100 rounded flex items-center gap-3 transition-colors <%= 'bg-cream-100' if search_mode == mode %>">
                <i class="bi <%= icon %> text-muted"></i>
                <div>
                  <div class="font-medium"><%= label %></div>
                  <div class="text-[10px] text-muted"><%= description %></div>
                </div>
                <% if search_mode == mode %>
                  <i class="bi bi-check2 text-heading ml-auto"></i>
                <% end %>
              </button>
            <% end %>
          </div>
        <% end %>
      </div>

    <%# The tool of the view (20a, S2): the column picker's trigger on the
          ticket list, nothing on the knowledge list. Flat like "+ Filter", for
          the same reason. %>
      <% if view_tool? %>
        <div class="flex-shrink-0" data-fb-view-tool><%= view_tool %></div>
      <% end %>

    </div>

    <%# Filter Menu (Level 1: categories), a floating layer (F29). A dialog,
        not a menu: it opens with a head that holds a close, and a menu may own
        nothing but its items. The list inside keeps role="menu", so the arrow
        keys still walk it. Head and list are built by the controller, in the
        same place as the head of level 2, so the two cannot drift.

        It hangs at the bar's root and is placed by the controller, because two
        triggers open it: "+ Filter" up here, and "+ Bedingung" down in the
        condition row (20a, § 6). A layer nailed to one of them would open in
        the wrong place for the other. %>
    <div data-filter-bar-target="filterMenu"
         role="dialog"
         aria-modal="false"
         aria-label="<%= scoped_t('filter_bar.add_filter') %>"
         class="hidden absolute w-56 bg-surface-raised border border-cream-300 rounded-lg shadow-md z-dropdown">
      <div data-filter-bar-target="categoryList"></div>
    </div>

    <%# Filter Value Menu (Level 2). It sits inside row 1 but is positioned
        against the controller root, the nearest positioned ancestor: the row
        container must never become position: relative. A dialog: the
        controller names it after the category and moves the focus in and out. %>
    <div data-filter-bar-target="valueMenu"
         role="dialog"
         aria-modal="false"
         class="hidden absolute w-60 bg-surface-raised border border-cream-300 rounded-lg shadow-md z-dropdown">
    </div>

  </div>

  <%# The menu of the active view (S5): a floating list (F29, F33) under the
      chevron, positioned by the controller against the bar's root (the strip
      clips what overflows it). Entries appear only where the policy allows;
      rename happens in this layer, the destructive entry sits under a divider
      (F27), the expert filter opens the unchanged modal (F34: it opens
      something else). A dialog, not a menu: it holds a form (the rename), and a
      menu may own only items; the controller moves the focus in and out. %>
  <div data-filter-bar-target="viewMenu"
       role="dialog"
       aria-modal="false"
       aria-label="<%= t('components.filter_bar.view_menu') %>"
       data-view-name="<%= view_menu[:name] %>"
       data-rename-url="<%= view_menu[:rename_url] %>"
       data-delete-url="<%= view_menu[:delete_url] %>"
       class="hidden absolute w-60 bg-surface-raised border border-cream-300 rounded-lg shadow-md z-dropdown p-1">
    <div data-filter-bar-target="viewMenuList">
      <% if view_menu[:rename_url] %>
        <button type="button"
                data-action="click->filter-bar#startRename"
                class="<%= MENU_ROW_CLASSES %>"><%= t('components.filter_bar.rename') %></button>
      <% end %>
      <% if view_menu[:share_url] %>
        <a href="<%= view_menu[:share_url] %>"
           class="<%= MENU_ROW_CLASSES %>"><%= t('components.filter_bar.share') %></a>
      <% end %>
      <% if view_menu[:duplicate_url] %>
        <button type="button"
                data-action="click->filter-bar#duplicateView"
                data-url="<%= view_menu[:duplicate_url] %>"
                class="<%= MENU_ROW_CLASSES %>"><%= t('components.filter_bar.duplicate_view') %></button>
      <% end %>
      <a href="<%= view_menu[:expert_url] %>"
         data-turbo-frame="modal"
         data-action="click->filter-bar#carryReturnContext click->filter-bar#closeAllMenus"
         class="<%= MENU_ROW_CLASSES %>"><%= t('components.filter_bar.open_expert_filter') %></a>
      <% if view_menu[:delete_url] %>
        <div class="border-t border-divider my-1" role="separator"></div>
        <button type="button"
                data-action="click->filter-bar#deleteView"
                class="<%= MENU_ROW_CLASSES %> text-red-700 hover:text-red-900"><%= t('components.filter_bar.delete_view') %></button>
      <% end %>
    </div>
    <% if view_menu[:rename_url] %>
      <form data-filter-bar-target="renameForm"
            data-action="submit->filter-bar#submitRename"
            class="hidden flex-wrap items-center gap-2 p-1">
        <input type="text" name="name"
               value="<%= view_menu[:name] %>"
               data-filter-bar-target="renameInput"
               aria-label="<%= t('components.filter_bar.rename') %>"
               aria-describedby="filter-bar-rename-error"
               autocomplete="off" required maxlength="255"
               class="h-8 flex-1 min-w-0 px-2 text-xs rounded-md border border-cream-300 bg-surface-raised text-body
                      focus:outline-none focus:border-ink focus:ring-2 focus:ring-ink/10">
        <button type="submit" data-fb-word
                class="<%= TEXT_ACTION_CLASSES %>"><%= t('components.filter_bar.rename_save') %></button>
        <button type="button" data-fb-word
                data-action="click->filter-bar#cancelRename"
                class="<%= TEXT_ACTION_CLASSES %>"><%= t('components.filter_bar.rename_cancel') %></button>
        <%# The server's reason for a refused name (blank, too long) lands here;
            empty and hidden until then. %>
        <p id="filter-bar-rename-error" data-filter-bar-target="renameError"
           class="hidden basis-full text-xs text-red-700"></p>
      </form>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <%# === ROW 2a: the conditions as a sentence (20a, S1). This is the resting
      state: a filter is read many times and changed once. The values are the
      only targets in it, because changing one value is the commonest move and
      needs no change of form; "ändern" opens the whole condition row below.

      The sentence is built on the server (FilterSentenceService), so the rule
      exists once and can be tested; the frame lets an edit leave it alone and
      the end of the edit refresh it, one request per editing session instead
      of one per tick. === %>
  <turbo-frame id="<%= sentence_frame_id %>" data-filter-bar-target="sentenceFrame">
    <div class="<%= 'hidden' unless has_any_chips? %>" data-filter-bar-target="sentenceRow">
      <%# Without a condition there is no sentence, and then there is no row:
          "ändern" on its own says nothing and would still take a line. The
          way in without a condition is "+ Filter" up in the tab row (§ 7). %>
      <%# text-wrap: pretty keeps the last line from carrying a single word, and
          the nbsp before "ändern" keeps it off the middle of the sentence. %>
      <% unless filter_sentence.empty? %>
      <p class="<%= SENTENCE_PROSE_CLASSES %>" data-fb-prose
         title="<%= filter_sentence.to_s %>"><%= sentence_html %>&nbsp;<button type="button"
              data-action="click->filter-bar#startEditing"
              data-filter-bar-target="editWord"
              class="<%= TEXT_ACTION_CLASSES %> whitespace-nowrap"><%= t('components.filter_bar.edit_conditions') %></button></p>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </turbo-frame>

  <%# The selection row, if the list has one: it takes the sentence's place
      while rows are ticked (D2 of doc/ticket_bulk_edit_plan.md). Hidden until
      the list's selection controller shows it; the controller hides the
      sentence frame at the same time. %>
  <%= selection_row if selection_row? %>

  <%# === ROW 2b: one pill per condition, the editing state. The row is gone,
      not collapsed, while nothing is being edited. === %>
  <div class="hidden"
       data-filter-bar-target="chipRow">
    <%# The SECOND LINE of the tab row's surface, exactly where the sentence
        stands when nothing is being edited - it replaces that line, it does not
        come on top of it. No line of its own above or below: the tab row has
        one, and the surface's own bottom edge separates it from the table.
        ps-3 starts the first chip under the FIRST TAB's word (designer,
        07.09.2026); it used to begin ~22px further left, which is a second left
        edge in two consecutive lines. %>
    <%# pe-3 mirrors the ps-3: the count sits at the far end of the row, and
        without it the last thing in the row touches the surface's edge. %>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 ps-3 pe-3 pt-2 pb-1 min-w-0">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 min-w-0"
           data-filter-bar-target="chipZone"
           id="filter-bar-chips">
        <%# Pills are rendered by the Stimulus controller from the effective conditions %>
      </div>
      <%# "+ Bedingung" (20a, § 6): the dashed edge says "something is being
          made here". It is not "+ Filter" and does not read like it: that one
          means START filtering and stands in the tab row, this one means take
          ONE more and stands where the conditions are. %>
      <button type="button"
              data-action="click->filter-bar#toggleFilterMenu"
              data-fb-add-condition
              aria-haspopup="dialog"
              aria-expanded="false"
              class="h-7 px-2.5 text-[13px] font-normal rounded-full border border-dashed border-cream-400 text-body
                     hover:border-ink hover:text-heading transition-colors inline-flex items-center gap-1.5
                     focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ink">
        <span aria-hidden="true">+</span> <%= t('components.filter_bar.add_condition') %>
      </button>

      <%# "fertig" ends the editing state, it saves nothing. Saving happens in
          the row below, and only where something differs from the view.
          Right behind "+ Bedingung" (user, 08.09.2026): both are things one
          DOES to the row of conditions, and one more and I am done belong next
          to each other. Not underlined at rest - a permanent underline over the
          table makes a quiet word the loudest thing in the row; the underline
          arrives on hover, where it says "this is a link". %>
      <button type="button" data-fb-word
              data-action="click->filter-bar#stopEditing"
              class="text-xs font-medium text-muted hover:text-heading hover:underline underline-offset-2
                     focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-ink rounded"><%= t('components.filter_bar.done_editing') %></button>

    </div>
  </div>

  <%# The proposal row (F31, S6): something outside proposes a condition and the
      reader has not decided. Its own row under the conditions with the source
      as a mark, the sentence, and two words. Never a pill in the condition
      row: a pill there claims it already filters. "Übernehmen" makes a normal
      condition of it (the view differs, the save row appears); "Ablehnen"
      removes the row. Nothing is persisted here; a producer that wants to
      remember a decline gets a callback later. %>
  <div data-filter-bar-target="proposalRow" class="<%= 'hidden' if proposal_rows.empty? %>">
    <% proposal_rows.each do |proposal| %>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 border-t border-divider py-2 text-xs text-body"
           data-proposal
           data-category="<%= proposal[:category] %>"
           data-value="<%= proposal[:value] %>">
        <span class="text-[9.5px] uppercase tracking-wider border border-cream-300 rounded px-1.5 text-muted flex-shrink-0"><%= proposal[:source] %></span>
        <span class="mr-auto" data-fb-sentence><%= t('components.filter_bar.proposal_question_html', condition: tag.strong(proposal[:condition], class: 'font-semibold text-heading')) %></span>
        <button type="button" data-fb-word
                data-action="click->filter-bar#acceptProposal"
                class="<%= TEXT_ACTION_CLASSES %>"><%= t('components.filter_bar.accept') %></button>
        <button type="button" data-fb-word
                data-action="click->filter-bar#declineProposal"
                class="<%= TEXT_ACTION_CLASSES %>"><%= t('components.filter_bar.decline') %></button>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <%# === ROW 3: the save row (F23), filled by the controller while the state
      differs from the view. Under the conditions, never between tabs and
      conditions: appearing must not push away what was just touched. === %>
  <%# The live region is this persistent element, not the row the controller
      renders into it: assistive tech announces a change of content, and the
      sentence changes here with every edit. %>
  <div data-filter-bar-target="saveRow" class="hidden" aria-live="polite"></div>

  <%# The flash the controller shows after a save or a discard (F25). Rendered
      by NeoFlashComponent so its look lives in one place; the controller clones
      it, sets the message and, where something was thrown away, the way back. %>
  <template data-filter-bar-target="flashTemplate">
    <%= render NeoFlashComponent.new(type: :success, message: 'message', hide_delay: 2500) %>
  </template>
  <template data-filter-bar-target="errorFlashTemplate">
    <%= render NeoFlashComponent.new(type: :error, message: 'message', hide_delay: 4000) %>
  </template>
</div>
